2,Understanding the importance of Tibetan music,https://www.tibettravel.org/tibetan-culture/understanding-the-importance-of-tibetan-music.html,"May 6, 2025 - You will find that flutes and lutes combine with some percussion beats to create a soft aroma of music that is thought to resemble a constant communication link with the divine world, one that only ""perfect beings"" are able to compose. It is officially named Sino-Mongolian music and is heard in the streets during festivals and parties.",Phuza,Sino-Tibetan
3,Songs and Music of Tibet | Smithsonian Folkways Recordings,https://folkways.si.edu/songs-and-music-of-tibet/world/album/smithsonian,"From a camp in the outskirts of Kathmandu, Howard Kaufman captures the essence of Tibetan chants. Kaufman gathers songs that are ""excerpts from much longer versions of both Eastern and Western Tibet"".",Phuza,Sino-Tibetan
